  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/stat/84/1417" ;
  fro-usc:hasSourceCreditText "( Aug. 22, 1940, ch. 686 ; Pub. L. 100–181, title VI , § 610, Dec. 4, 1987 , 101 Stat. 1261 ; Pub. L. 104–290, title II , § 202, Oct. 11, 1996 , 110 Stat. 3426 ; Pub. L. 105–353, title III , § 301(c)(3), Nov. 3, 1998 , 112 Stat. 3236 ; Pub. L. 111–203, title IX , title I, § 12, 54 Stat. 808 , § 985(d)(3), July 21, 2010 , 124 Stat. 1934 .) ; Pub. L. 91–547 , § 7, Dec. 14, 1970 , 84 Stat. 1417" ;
.
usc-t15-ch2D:idd0437447-0c74-11e6-aa53-e455a13f2ad9
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Note ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 0 ;
  fro-ref:hasSourceInstance <http://finregont.com/fro/usc/USC-2015-title15-chapter2D.ttl#r-1-0-4-3-14-10-0> ;
  fro-usc:hasHeading "References in Text" ;
  fro-usc:hasId "idd0437447-0c74-11e6-aa53-e455a13f2ad9" ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "The Securities Exchange Act of 1934, referred to in subsec. (d)(1)(B), (E)(i), is act June 6, 1934, ch. 404 , 48 Stat. 881 , as amended, which is classified generally to 2B (§ 78a et seq.) of this title. For complete classification of this Act to the Code, see section 78a of this title and Tables." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteTopic "referencesInText" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/act/1934-06-06/ch404" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/stat/48/881" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/usc/t15/s78a" ;
.
usc-t15-ch2D:idd0437448-0c74-11e6-aa53-e455a13f2ad9
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Note ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 1 ;
  fro-ref:hasSourceInstance <http://finregont.com/fro/usc/USC-2015-title15-chapter2D.ttl#r-1-0-4-3-14-10-1> ;
  fro-usc:hasHeading "Amendments" ;
  fro-usc:hasId "idd0437448-0c74-11e6-aa53-e455a13f2ad9" ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "1970—Subsec. (d)(1). Pub. L. 91–547 substituted provisions designated as subpars. (A) to (C) and (E) to (H) for former introductory provisions reading “It shall be unlawful for any registered investment company and any company or companies controlled by such registered investment company to purchase or otherwise acquire after August 22, 1940 , any security issued by or any other interest in the business of—” and subpar. (1) reading “any other investment company of which such registered investment company and company or companies controlled by such registered company shall not at the time of such purchase or acquisition own in the aggregate at least 25 per centum of the total outstanding voting stock, if such registered investment company and any company or companies controlled by it own in the aggregate or as a result of such purchase or acquisition will own in the aggregate more than 5 per centum of the total outstanding voting stock of such other investment company if the policy of such other investment company is the concentration of investments in a particular industry or group of industries, or more than 3 per centum of the total outstanding voting stock of such other investment company if the policy of such other investment company is not the concentration of investments in a particular industry or group of industries, except and cl. (B) exception reading “a security purchased with the proceeds of payments on periodic payment plan certificates, pursuant to the terms of the trust indenture under which such certificates are issued”, cl. (A) of such subpar. (1) being incorporated in subpar. (D) of this par. (1)." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "1987—Subsec. (d)(1)(A)(iii). Pub. L. 100–181 , § 610(1), substituted “treasury” for “Treasury”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "1996—Subsec. (d)(1)(D), (E). Pub. L. 104–290 , § 202(3), substituted “this paragraph” for “this paragraph (1)”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "1998—Subsec. (d)(1)(G)(i)(III)(bb). Pub. L. 105–353 substituted “the acquired company” for “the acquired fund”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "2010—Subsec. (d)(1)(J). Pub. L. 111–203 substituted “any provision of this paragraph” for “any provision of this subsection”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Pub. L. 104–290 , § 202(2), redesignated subpar. (G) as (H). Former subpar. (H) redesignated (I)." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Pub. L. 104–290 , § 202(2), redesignated subpar. (H) as (I)." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (d)(1)(E)(iii)(bb). Pub. L. 104–290 , § 202(1)(B), inserted “in the event that such investment company is not a registered investment company,” after “(bb)”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (d)(1)(E)(iii). Pub. L. 104–290 , § 202(1)(A), struck out “in the event such investment company is not a registered investment company,” after “(iii)”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (d)(1)(F). Pub. L. 104–290 , § 202(3), substituted “this paragraph” for “this paragraph (1)”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (d)(1)(G). Pub. L. 100–181 , § 610(2), substituted “is reasonably possible” for “it reasonably possible”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (d)(1)(G). Pub. L. 104–290 , § 202(2), (4), added subpar. (G). Former subpar. (G) redesignated (H)." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (d)(1)(H). Pub. L. 104–290 , § 202(3), substituted “this paragraph” for “this paragraph (1)”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (d)(1)(I). Pub. L. 104–290 , § 202(3), substituted “this paragraph” for “this paragraph (1)” wherever appearing." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (d)(1)(J). Pub. L. 104–290 , § 202(5), added subpar. (J)." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (d)(2). Pub. L. 91–547 incorporated existing introductory text and subpar. (2) provisions in provisions redesignated as par. (2) and struck out “after August 22, 1940 ,” after “purchase or otherwise acquire”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (d)(3). Pub. L. 91–547 incorporated existing introductory text and subpar. (3) provisions in provisions redesignated as par. (3) and struck out “after August 22, 1940 ,” after “purchase or otherwise acquire”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteText "Subsec. (f). Pub. L. 100–181 , § 610(3), substituted “thereof only” for “only thereof”." ;
  fro-usc:hasNoteTopic "amendments" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/pl/100/181" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/pl/104/290" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/pl/105/353" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/pl/111/203" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/pl/91/547" ;
.
